In the Left/Right question format, 0 represents the left response, and 1 represents the right.

Each key corresponds to a set of 8 questions, with responses stored as bits. The position of each bit within the answer byte indicates the identity of the question in the set, numbered 1 through 8. A 0 in the answer byte signifies the left response, and a 1 signifies the right.

For unanswered questions, a second byte, the null-check byte, is used. Each answered question is marked as 1 in the null-check byte.

An unanswered question is represented by a 0 in the answer byte.

If all questions in a set are answered, the null-check byte can be omitted.
If all questions are unanswered, both bytes can be omitted, and null is returned


